"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-07T23:21:32Z","updated_at":"2024-11-07T23:23:10Z","body":"> problem: - entry level writing style, tedious to read\r\n\r\nThis is not a problem.\r\n\r\nMost of the \"solutions\" in this PR are in fact a \"problem\".\r\n\r\nCode should be first of all easy to understand.\r\n\r\nTedious and easy >> Fancy and cryptic.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463416988/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":7,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2464501545","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98941#issuecomment-2464501545","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98941","id":2464501545,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6S5U8p","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-08T11:38:33Z","updated_at":"2024-11-08T11:38:47Z","body":"Thanks for the contribution, but I don't think it's a positive improvement to the code quality.\r\n\r\nThe main change done here is changing this kind of pattern which we use intentionally:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (cond1) {\r\n  return true;\r\n}\r\n\r\nif (cond2) {\r\n  return true;\r\n}\r\n\r\nif (cond3) {\r\n  return true;\r\n}\r\n\r\nreturn false;\r\n```\r\nTo this:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (cond1) {\r\n  return true;\r\n}\r\n\r\nif (cond2) {\r\n  return true;\r\n}\r\n\r\nreturn cond3;\r\n```\r\n\r\nSure, technically this is correct. But the intention of the code was clear that we're checking a list of conditions, which may be expanded in the future, and that the function ends with the default return value if none of the previous checks passed.\r\n\r\nBreaking this pattern is not an improvement to code quality in this codebase.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2464501545/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]